# Product Rules

## Brand

**TAKELEY** (테이클리 — TAKE + DAILY)

Tagline: **Take a look. Take a side.**

## One-line definition

AI finds Issues people care about, turns them into short cards, and lets users leave a take and see others — not a news dump, not an X translator bot, not a finance terminal.

## Core loop

```text
DISCOVER → UNDERSTAND → TAKE → RETURN
```

## Success looks like

“이 이슈, 어떻게 생각해? — 한 번 누르고 남들 생각도 본다.”  
Not “정보가 많다.” / Not “오늘 브리핑 들었다.”

## MVP focus

High-quality daily Issues (~5–10), multi-source when possible.  
Loop: **Card → Take → See others / comments**.  
Validate participation rate over polish features.

## Trend status (NORMAL | RISING | TRENDING)

External fame alone is not enough. RISING / TRENDING require **external signal** (velocity or AI+reply peak) **and** TAKELEY internal interest (unique opens / follow / vote).  
RISING = rising speed; TRENDING = larger scale. Comments are not required. No separate HOT state.

## Non-goals (for now)

- Tweet reposting / content-formatter posting flows
- Full-market Bloomberg / HTS coverage
- Per-request live web search + LLM answers
- Social graph (follow, DM, friends)
- Prediction markets / money / points / heavy gamification
- Forced debate on every announcement
- UI redesign in identity-only migrations

## When implementing features

Ask: does this help someone understand an Issue fast and express a view?  
If it only adds more raw posts, charts, or dashboard chrome, skip it.
